# CLAUDE.local.md — personal notes

> Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` at the repo root. The real file
> is gitignored, so anything you put in it stays on your machine.
>
>     cp CLAUDE.local.md.example CLAUDE.local.md
>
> Claude Code picks up both `CLAUDE.md` (committed, shared project
> instructions) and `CLAUDE.local.md` (personal, gitignored) at the
> start of every session.

This is *your* scratchpad. Anything here is context Claude will have
on hand without you having to re-explain it. Treat it like a pinned
note, not a spec — short, personal, always up to date.

Suggested sections below. Delete any you don't want.

---

